{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774195877,"nonce":"Xq13k7RK9ZtC/ZK5L66Farq/7zg=","title":"SDK-mediated subagent spawning: replace Agent tool with Mandible-managed sessions","message":"Replace Claude Code's built-in Agent tool with Mandible-managed SDK sessions to enable richer subagent interaction: live observation, bidirectional communication, and independent lifecycle control.\n\n**The problem with the Agent tool:**\n- Subagents run as internal loops within the parent query — no independent lifecycle control\n- Events are interleaved in the parent stream (filtered by parent_tool_use_id) — no dedicated stream\n- Users cannot interact with running subagents — read-only observation only\n- No way to pause, resume, or redirect a specific subagent independently\n\n**The SDK makes replacement feasible:**\nThe @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk Options.agents parameter (Record\u003cstring, AgentDefinition\u003e) allows programmatic subagent definitions. When Mandible spawns sessions via SDKBackend, it can define custom agents that route through Mandible rather than the built-in Agent tool. Each subagent becomes its own SDK query() session with:\n- Dedicated event stream (separate WebSocket)\n- Independent lifecycle (start/stop/destroy/interrupt)\n- Direct sendPrompt() for user interaction\n- Permission gating via canUseTool callback\n- Separate cost tracking\n\n**Two complementary approaches:**\n\nApproach A — MCP tool (mandible_spawn_agent):\n- Register an MCP tool on the channel server that the parent agent calls instead of Agent\n- Mandible spawns an independent SDK session\n- Streams events to dashboard in real time\n- Returns final result as tool_result to parent\n- Parent instructions (CLAUDE.md/preset) direct it to prefer this tool over built-in Agent\n- Optional: disallowedTools: [\"Agent\"] to force all delegation through Mandible\n\nApproach B — Custom agents parameter:\n- When Mandible spawns sessions via SDKBackend, pass agents definitions that wrap Mandible\n- Each defined agent spawns through Mandible's infrastructure rather than Claude Code's internal loop\n- Preserves the Agent tool interface but routes execution through Mandible\n\n**User interaction with subagents:**\nWith SDK-mediated spawning, each subagent is its own ConsoleSession. Users can:\n- View live activity in a dedicated chat panel (not filtered from parent stream)\n- Send messages to running subagents via sendPrompt()\n- Course-correct mid-task without stopping the whole build\n- Approve/deny permissions independently per subagent\n\n**Key technical constraint:**\nThe SDK's PreToolUse hook cannot fully replace Agent tool execution — it can gate or modify input, but cannot substitute a different execution path. So interception is not viable; the approaches above (MCP tool or agents parameter) are the correct integration points.\n\n**Relationship to other issues:**\n- 1b88786: Live sidebar observation works for both Agent-tool and SDK-mediated subagents, but SDK-mediated enables interaction\n- 781f473: Subagent result pruning is independent — applies to whatever mechanism returns results to parent\n- aea2c67: Console architecture already supports SDK sessions with all needed infrastructure","files":null}]}